ndlord will have no Jokers. This means playing a 2 secures the trick or forces a bomb.\n\n**Final Decision**\n\nI\'m going to play a single ♥2. It is an optimal play to beat the Ace and force control of the lead.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The Landlord led with an Ace. As the "guard" (the peasant playing immediately after the Landlord), my role is to block the Landlord\'s high cards to protect my teammate and seize the initiative. I have an extremely strong hand containing the Rocket (both Jokers), a pair of 2s, and pairs of Aces and Kings. Crucially, because I hold both Jokers, the Landlord cannot have any Jokers. This means my 2 is the highest possible single card (invincible unless the Landlord uses a Bomb).\n\nReason: Playing the 2 guarantees winning the trick (unless the Landlord uses a Bomb, which is a good trade). This stops the Landlord from gaining momentum and gives me the lead to start playing out my smaller cards (singles like 3, 7, 8, 9, Q or small pairs). Passing would be passive and might force my teammate to break their hand structure to deal with the Ace.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥2"]}'}
