tion, beats everything.\n        13. Quadplex set: a quad with two single cards OR two pairs attached.\n        Use the EXACT card symbols provided in the Valid Moves list.\n        Prepare a valid JSON object like {"cards": ["♠3", "♥3"]} for your answer, along with your explanation and reason. If you pass, output: {"cards": []}\n        \n        Now is your turn, to your best ability, choose your move to maximize your chances of winning.\n        Please briefly evaluate a few proimsing moves, provide reason for your final choice, and output the action with specified format.\n        Your response format should be:\n        Evaluation: [Your Evaluation]\n        Reason: [Your Reason]\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\n    ', 'user_prompt': "You are playing as a peasant. Your aim is to be the play out all your cards before the landlord does, OR help your teammate (the other peasant) play out their cards before the landlord does. If the landlord plays out all cards first, you lose.\nYou are a Peasant. The Next Player (Right) is the Landlord (ENEMY). The Previous Player (Left) is your TEAMMATE (Peasant). You must cooperate with your teammate to beat the Landlord. The objective is to empty your hand before the landlord does, or help your teammate empty their hand before the landlord does.\n\nYour Hand: ♣9 ♠Q BlackJoker RedJoker\nLast Play to Beat: None (Free Play)\n--- Game History (Recent) ---\nTurn 9 (You): ♣2\nTurn 10 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 10 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 10 (You): ♠8\nTurn 11 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 11 (Prev Player): ♠A\nTurn 11 (You): Pass\nTurn 12 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 12 (Prev Player): ♥Q ♦Q\nTurn 12 (You): ♠K ♦K\nTurn 13 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 13 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 13 (You): ♥A ♣A\nTurn 14 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 14 (Prev Player): Pass\n--- Player Info ---\nCards Held by Next Player (Right) [Landlord (Opponent)]: 18\nCards Held by Prev Player (Left) [Peasant (Teammate)]: 1\n--- Cards Remaining Unknown (Card Counting) ---\n(Format explanation: 'Rank: Count', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\n2: 2, K: 1, Q: 1, J: 1, 9: 2, 8: 2, 7: 3, 6: 2, 5: 1, 4: 2, 3: 2\nValid Moves:\nsingle: ♣9\nsingle: ♠Q\nsingle: BlackJoker\nsingle: RedJoker\nrocket: BlackJoker RedJoker\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': "**Analysis and Strategy: Fight the Landlord**\n\nAlright, let's break this down. My teammate has one card left, the Landlord has a hefty eighteen. My hand? I've got a 9, a Queen, and the Rocket (Black and Red Jokers).  We're in a prime spot here, a chance to really force the win.\n\nI need to facilitate my teammate, but I can't just throw anything out there. If I just toss out my Queen, the Landlord could come in with something I can't beat and then we are stuck.  The Rocket is a trump card, but only if used properly. I have to avoid a situation where I lose control and the Landlord goes on a run I can't touch.\n\nThe ideal is for my teammate to win this turn.\n\nIf the Landlord plays a high card, my teammate is blocked, so that's no good. A low card? The teammate might be able to win with their final card.\n\nThe best strategy here is the safest, and most likely to work! I've gotta play the **9**.  If the Landlord passes, my teammate wins.  If the Landlord plays something low, maybe my teammate has something to beat it. If the Landlord plays high? Then I have the Rocket. That's the key. I can blast away whatever the Landlord throws down, and then play my Queen. Then I win. The game is over.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: I hold a guaranteed winning hand (Rocket + two singles) against a Landlord with many cards, and my teammate has only 1 card left. My primary goal is to let the teammate win immediately by playing a low single. If the Landlord blocks, I can use the Rocket to regain the lead and finish my own hand.\nReason: Playing the lowest single (9) gives the teammate (who has 1 card) the best chance to beat the card and win the game instantly. If the Landlord plays a high card to block the teammate, I will use the Rocket to take control and then play my remaining Queen to empty my hand and win. This strategy covers all contingencies.\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣9"]}'}
